  "name": "Liquid Dark Reese",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "The dark rolling reese: two detuned saw voices beating slowly against each other under a warm low-pass, with a clean sub underneath. A living low drone for halftime drops and long held notes. Play F1 to A#1 as sustained notes at 140 to 150 BPM and listen to the slow beat inside the note. Beat widens the detuning and brightens it a touch, Darkness opens the filter, Drift deepens a one-bar filter sweep and Warmth pushes tube saturation for harmonics.",
